{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added the per-user feed limit (`max_feeds`, 0 = unlimited). The build and the existing unit and integration tests pass; the new behaviour itself is not covered by any test I could run.\n\n- **Schema and model:** a new migration adds `users.max_feeds int not null default 0`. The field is on `model.User`, `model.UserModificationRequest` and the Go client's equivalents, and is read and written by all user queries in `internal/storage/user.go`.\n- **Enforcement:** `Storage.CreateFeed` now locks the user row, counts the user's feeds and inserts in one transaction, returning `storage.ErrFeedLimitReached` without creating anything when the limit is hit. Because every creation path goes through it, the limit also applies to the web UI and the Google Reader API, not only to the two endpoints named in the task.\n- **`POST /v1/feeds`:** returns 400 when the limit is reached, checked once before fetching the feed and again at insert.\n- **`POST /v1/import`:** imports feeds until the limit is reached, then stops and returns 400. Feeds imported before that point are kept, so the import is partial rather than all-or-nothing.\n- **`PUT /v1/users/{userID}`:** a non-admin request that includes `max_feeds` gets 403, even if the value is unchanged. A negative value gets 400.\n\nOne thing to be aware of: in the web UI and Google Reader paths the limit error surfaces as the generic database error message, since I did not add a new translation key to the locale files.", "t": 1794463783.136}
{"tool": "_result", "name": "finish", "chars": 55, "t": 1794463783.14}
